XIF - END ALL IFS WHEN CURRENT STATE IS TRUE

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
XIF - END ALL IFS WHEN CURRENT STATE IS TRUE

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    XIF

Ends all active IF levels only when the current IF state is true. In a
false state it leaves the conditional tree in place.

Use FI to close one level. ZIF clears the whole tree regardless of state,
so it is the deliberate recovery command for a stuck false branch.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
